<Project>

  <!-- WHERE A BUILD'S COMMIT COMES FROM (RECOVERY-PHASES P2.6).

       These become [assembly: AssemblyMetadata("DodonaCommit", "...")] on every project that
       compiles Ver.cs, and Ver reads them back at runtime. FIELDS WE NAMED, holding ONE plain
       value each.

       THE FIRST ATTEMPT PUT THIS IN AssemblyInformationalVersion, WHICH WAS A MISTAKE. Both
       of its failures came from sharing a field the toolchain also writes:

         1. the value was one comma separated string, and the dotnet CLI SPLITS the value of a
            command line property on commas. It arrived truncated at the first comma, losing
            the main baseline and the trial flag, with no error anywhere.
         2. the SDK appends its own SourceRevisionId to InformationalVersion in a git checkout,
            so the value came back with extra text glued on. The SDK also writes a bare commit
            SHA there by itself, which any "is it non empty?" test would have believed.

       Separate named keys have none of that: nothing else writes them, there is no shared
       string to compose, and there is no format to parse, so there is no parser to get wrong.

       A build with no DodonaCommit has NO provenance: a plain "dev build", or a publish of an
       already built binary, which compiled nothing and so knows nothing. Every consumer must
       treat that as "unknown" and never as "behind". The old code silently degraded to an
       mtime compare in exactly that case, which is the loop prone bug wearing a fallback.

       XML COMMENTS CANNOT CONTAIN A DOUBLE DASH, which is why this file spells flags out in
       words. MSBuild refuses to load the whole file otherwise, and every project in the tree
       then fails with MSB4024 rather than anything mentioning this file's real subject. -->

  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(DodonaCommit)' != ''">
    <AssemblyMetadata Include="DodonaCommit" Value="$(DodonaCommit)" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(DodonaMainSha)' != ''">
    <AssemblyMetadata Include="DodonaMainSha" Value="$(DodonaMainSha)" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(DodonaDirty)' != ''">
    <AssemblyMetadata Include="DodonaDirty" Value="$(DodonaDirty)" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(DodonaBranch)' != ''">
    <AssemblyMetadata Include="DodonaBranch" Value="$(DodonaBranch)" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
